  "title": "Rainwater saving and use in households, Bremen",
  "summary": "To reduce pressure on its sewage system, Bremen has taken new approaches in rainwater management. Fee refunds and subsidies were the main success factor for the adoption of rainwater-based solutions by households (e.g. for toilets, garden irrigation, and collection tanks). In Germany, for a long time a single fee for both rainwater and wastewater was levied in all communities. After some German court decisions the fee for rainwater was separated from wastewater one and is now based on the extension of impervious property surface (m 2 ), which directs water into the public sewage system. Collecting rainwater on private property with e.g.",
